{"ts": "2026-08-17T11:01:26Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 52, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "commit 12423bd5cf11439d63bd3777a5815e02fe454314\nAuthor: test-project <dev@test-project.local>\nDate:   Mon Aug 17 10:46:54 2026 +0000\n\n    Edit a task title (Taiga #3)\n    \n    Built by the role pipeline. Verified independently: backend 14 passed, 2 warnings in 0.05s; build \u2713 built in 91ms; e2e 30 passed in 17.55s\n\n frontend/src/App.css                 | 15 ++++++\n frontend/src/App.jsx                 |  3 ++\n frontend/src/api.js                  |  2 +\n frontend/src/components/TaskList.jsx | 96 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----\n 4 files changed, 104 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)\n\ncommit 7e4f0a881704d49c12e1e0bd083719b7e1eb397e\nAuthor: test-project <dev@test-project.local>\nDate:   Mon Aug 17 09:10:28 2026 +0000\n\n    Filter tasks by done state (Taiga #1)\n    \n    Adds an all/open/done filter above the task list. Built end to end by the\n    role pipeline: story, design, a parallel frontend/backend build, three review\n    passes and two test passes.\n    \n    TaskFilter is a new component following the project's one-component-per-file\n    convention, with aria-pressed carrying the active state rather than colour\n    alone. Filtering happens in App from the tasks already loaded -- no new\n    endpoint, because the backend already returns everything needed and adding a\n    query parameter would have been API surface this feature does not require.\n    \n    TaskList now takes the filter so its empty state can say which filter is\n    hiding things, instead of claiming there is nothing to do when there is.\n    \n    The backend was correctly left untouched: the developer established that\n    Task.done, GET /api/tasks and POST /api/tasks/{id}/done already cover this,\n    and said so rather than inventing work for its scope.\n    \n    Verified independently of the agents' own reports: backend 8/8, frontend\n    builds, e2e 20/20 (12 browser tests added for the filter, including that a\n    filter survives adding and completing tasks while active).\n\n frontend/src/App.css                   | 19 +++++++++++++++++++\n frontend/src/App.jsx                   | 12 +++++++++++-\n frontend/src/components/TaskFilter.jsx | 23 +++++++++++++++++++++++\n frontend/src/components/TaskList.jsx   | 10 ++++++++--\n 4 files changed, 61 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)\n\ncommit 7c433e93d2bf0b8b343e8ca5299d7c15c7f9c1ba\nAuthor: test-project <dev@test-project.local>\nDate:   Mon Aug 17 08:17:46 2026 +0000\n\n    Scaffold the task-tracker app the pipeline builds against\n    \n    A React + FastAPI task tracker, small on purpose: every feature request in the\n    dogfood rounds should be implementable and verifiable in one cycle.\n    \n    CLAUDE.md states the conventions rather than leaving them implicit, because\n    the pipeline's roles are deliberately stack-agnostic and discover the stack\n    from the repo. This file is the thing they discover, so it is part of the\n    substrate being tested, not documentation about it.", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_012LU4CciCKQfrvsj84e27bq", "session_id": "96438b12-b321-4900-8b09-8b900d83292c"}}
