{"ts": "2026-08-17T11:03:06Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 165, "kind": "message", "text": "This matches the design exactly, one-to-one against `docs/design.md`'s specified diffs. The implementation is complete and verified.\n\n## Handoff\n\n**Frontend scope for Taiga #4 (give tasks a priority) \u2014 done.**\n\n**Files changed:**\n- `frontend/src/api.js` \u2014 `createTask(title, priority)` now sends `priority` in the POST body; added `setPriority(id, priority)` \u2192 `PATCH /api/tasks/{id}/priority`.\n- `frontend/src/components/AddTask.jsx` \u2014 added a `priority-select` (`Low`/`Normal`/`High`), defaulting to and resetting to `normal` after submit; `onAdd` now passes `(trimmed, priority)`.\n- `frontend/src/components/TaskList.jsx` \u2014 `TaskRow`'s view-mode row got a `priority-select` (independent of title-edit mode), threaded via a new `onPriorityChange` prop through `TaskList`.\n- `frontend/src/App.jsx` \u2014 added `sortedTasks`, a stable partition (`high` first) applied *after* the existing `visibleTasks` filter; `<TaskList>` now receives `sortedTasks` and a new `onPriorityChange` handler wired through the existing `run()`/`refresh()` pattern (no optimistic update, no new state machinery).\n- `frontend/src/App.css` \u2014 `.priority-select` base style plus `.priority-high` (orange fill/white text) and `.priority-low` (light gray) modifiers; `.priority-normal` intentionally has no override.\n\nAll changes match `docs/design.md` verbatim (component shapes, class names, colors, sort logic).\n\n**Verification run this session:**\n- `npm run build` (frontend) \u2014 clean, no errors.\n- `python3 -m pytest -q backend` \u2014 22 passed (parallel backend-scope agent already landed the `priority` field, `PATCH /api/tasks/{id}/priority`, validation, and tests \u2014 confirmed the contract my frontend code targets matches exactly).\n- `npm run lint` / `npx oxlint` \u2014 blocked by this session's permission allowlist (only `npm run build*`, `npm run dev*`, `npm test*`